From 02b58eefe0c9327226b22bd83653d4b2c5cc55cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:26:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Collect sparse matches one by one in ConstantScoreBulkScorer

ConstantScoreBulkScorer loads windows of 4096 doc IDs into a bit set, which it then
collects and clears. The cost of this is proportional to the size of the window rather
than to the number of matches in the window, so it is much more expensive than collecting
matches one by one when matches are far apart from each other: with a single match per
window, 64 longs get written, scanned and cleared for every match.

Plain iterators are now collected one by one for as long as fewer than 32 matches fit in
a window, and the bulk scorer only switches to bit sets where matches are closer to each
other. Two-phase iterators are not affected.

